{"event": "result", "result": {"conversation_id": "3188e3d9-e01d-4af8-abe7-83aed84b7265", "status": "SUCCESS", "response": "I have created the Python 3 and C polyglot file at [main.py.c](file:///tmp/xhs-c6-host-1ndw0a7c/polyglot/main.py.c) (mounted at `/app/polyglot/main.py.c` in the container).\n\n### How It Works\n- **Preprocessor & Multiline String Multiplexing**: `#if 0` / `#endif` blocks hide the Python string delimiters and Python implementation from `gcc`, while raw triple-quoted strings (`r\"\"\" ... \"\"\"`) and `#` comments hide the C `#include` directives and C implementation from `python3`.\n- **Fibonacci Implementation**: Both the C and Python sections parse `N` from `argv[1]` and compute $f(N)$ with $f(0) = 0, f(1) = 1$, supporting arbitrary-precision integers in both languages.\n", "duration_seconds": 74.932276241, "num_turns": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 22157, "output_tokens": 5210, "thinking_tokens": 3390, "cache_read_tokens": 52874, "total_tokens": 27367}}}